          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "y": 114.1,
            "text": "Chinese astrology organises years into cycles of 12, and asserts that the year you are born in affects your character. Each year is named after an animal. animal year characteristics 1 using situations for own benefit RAT 1972, 1984, imaginative, charming, generous, quick- 1 1996, 2008 tempered, opportunistic BUFFALO 1973, 1985, conservative, methodical2, conscientious, 1997, 2009 chauvinistic3, a born leader TIGER 1974, 1986, sensitive, emotional, tends to get carried 1998, 2010 away4, stubborn, rebellious, courageous RABBIT 1975, 1987, affectionate, obliging5, sentimental, 1999, 2011 superficial6, often insecure7 DRAGON 1976, 1988, fun-loving, popular, a perfectionist8, 2000, 2012 gifted, may sometimes be tactless9 SNAKE 1977, 1989, charming, intuitive10, stingy 2001, 2013 HORSE 1978, 1990, diligent11, independent, placid12, 2002, 2014 outgoing, can be selfish and cunning GOAT 1979, 1991, elegant, artistic, always ready to complain, 2003, 2015 over-anxious MONKEY 1980, 1992, witty, magnetic personality13, good 2004, 2016 company, can be distrustful14 ROOSTER 1981, 1993, industrious, shrewd15, supportive16, 2005, 2017 decisive, extravagant17 DOG 1982, 1994, down-to-earth18, altruistic19, morose20, 2006, 2018 sharp-tongued21 PIG 1983, 1995, intellectual, tolerant, naive22, often 2007, 2019 materialistic"
